{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrNyUdTFKun9ChZGtMxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open the repository, so this diagnosis rests on the snippets and on what I remember of the brocoders `nestjs-boilerplate` layout. The line numbers are estimates.\n\nThe error `needLoginViaProvider:google` comes from the login check. It rejects any user whose stored `provider` is not `email`. The user's stored provider must therefore be `google` even though they registered by email. The most likely cause is in the register flow, which should set `provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11245,"cache_read_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11245},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"86408fe0-2473-4f7c-b8eb-d15a907bcf61","uuid":"5edb1f99-a0c4-449b-91a2-1be2ecb45d67","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:07:15.918Z","request_id":"req_011CgrNyUT3SL4wuZbMqDNyq"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrNyUdTFKun9ChZGtMxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Msy2H5QSBd1VHQSfCq3uNE","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.register","start_line":100,"end_line":135,"explanation":"The register flow creates the user with the wrong provider. It should pass provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email to usersService.create but appears to store a different provider (google). validateLogin then rejects the user with needLoginViaProvider:<provider>, because the stored provider is not 'email'."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.validateLogin","start_line":55,"end_line":80,"explanation":"This is where the 422 `needLoginViaProvider:${user.provider}` is thrown. If the comparison against AuthProvidersEnum.email is wrong, or the user is looked up by the wrong key, a valid email user is rejected."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.confirmEmail","start_line":190,"end_line":230,"explanation":"Confirming the email may overwrite or reset the user's provider, for example by saving a user object with the wrong provider value. That would leave the user looking like a Google user right after confirmation."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In AuthService.register, create the user with provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email. Also check that confirmEmail only updates the user's status and does not touch provider."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11245,"cache_read_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11245},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pa